.TH REQUEST_KEY 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
request_key \- Linux x86-64 syscall 249
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_220_259.h>
.B long request_key(const char* type, const char* description, const char* callout, int keyring);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Requests a key from a Linux keyring.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR request_key (2)
